      "title": "Count crossings instead of solving a quintic",
      "body": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>120</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></math>. Its real roots are the crossings of the x-axis. Differentiate to find where the graph changes direction.</p>",
